# What cf push must NOT upload.
#
# Note the inversion against .gitignore: dist/ is ignored by git and is the one
# directory the platform actually needs, while node_modules and src are tracked
# concerns with no business on a static host.
#
# cf reads this file only. It does not fall back to .gitignore.
#
# Every source-tree entry below is anchored with a leading slash on purpose.
# .cfignore follows gitignore matching, where an unanchored `index.html` matches
# at any depth -- which would drop dist/index.html and publish a site whose
# entry point is a 404. Anchoring confines each pattern to the repo root.

/node_modules
/src
/public
/scripts
/index.html
/vite.config.js
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/manifest.yml

/.git
/.github
/.gitignore

/*.md
/*.patch
/*.diff

.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
npm-debug.log*
